## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates the ability to design robust input validation and data integrity checks for a privacy-centric API. It covers essential security concepts including replay protection, clock skew handling, cross-checks with cached values, and signature verification—all critical skills for building secure, reliable backend services.

## Key Concepts

- Input validation and schema enforcement
- Replay protection via nonce verification
- Clock skew tolerance and time synchronization
- Model version governance
- Score bounds validation
- Cross-checking against cached state for consistency
- Signature verification for authentication

## Code Example

```javascript
// POST /cca_score/validate
router.post('/cca_score/validate', async (req, res) => {
  const { masked_user_id, model_version, client_timestamp, cca_score, nonce, signature } = req.body;

  // 1. Presence and type validation
  if (!masked_user_id || !model_version || !client_timestamp || cca_score === undefined || !nonce || !signature) {
    return res.status(400).json({ error: 'MISSING_FIELDS', message: 'All required fields must be present' });
  }

  // 2. Replay protection - verify nonce is unique and not expired
  const nonceKey = `nonce:${masked_user_id}:${nonce}`;
  if (await redis.exists(nonceKey)) {
    return res.status(409).json({ error: 'REPLAY_DETECTED', message: 'Nonce has been used' });
  }
  await redis.setex(nonceKey, 300, '1'); // Store for 5 minutes

  // 3. Model version validation
  const knownVersions = ['v1.0', 'v1.1', 'v2.0'];
  if (!knownVersions.includes(model_version)) {
    return res.status(400).json({ error: 'UNKNOWN_MODEL_VERSION', message: 'Model version not supported' });
  }

  // 4. Clock skew tolerance (±5 minutes)
  const now = Date.now();
  const skewTolerance = 5 * 60 * 1000;
  if (Math.abs(now - client_timestamp) > skewTolerance) {
    return res.status(400).json({ error: 'CLOCK_SKEW', message: 'Client timestamp outside acceptable range' });
  }

  // 5. Score bounds validation (0-100)
  if (typeof cca_score !== 'number' || cca_score < 0 || cca_score > 100) {
    return res.status(400).json({ error: 'INVALID_SCORE', message: 'CCA score must be a number between 0 and 100' });
  }

  // 6. Cross-check with cached score (if available)
  const cachedScore = await redis.get(`cca_score:${masked_user_id}`);
  if (cachedScore !== null && Math.abs(cachedScore - cca_score) > 10) {
    return res.status(409).json({ error: 'SCORE_MISMATCH', message: 'Score significantly differs from cached value' });
  }

  // 7. Signature verification
  const payload = `${masked_user_id}:${model_version}:${client_timestamp}:${cca_score}:${nonce}`;
  const isValid = await verifySignature(signature, payload, masked_user_id);
  if (!isValid) {
    return res.status(401).json({ error: 'INVALID_SIGNATURE', message: 'Signature verification failed' });
  }

  // Success
  await redis.set(`cca_score:${masked_user_id}`, cca_score);
  return res.status(200).json({ status: 'valid', cca_score });
});
```

## Test Cases

```javascript
describe('POST /cca_score/validate', () => {
  it('should return 400 for missing fields', async () => {
    const res = await request(app).post('/cca_score/validate').send({ masked_user_id: 'user123' });
    expect(res.status).toBe(400);
    expect(res.body.error).toBe('MISSING_FIELDS');
  });

  it('should return 409 for replayed nonce', async () => {
    await redis.set('nonce:user123:testnonce', '1');
    const res = await request(app).post('/cca_score/validate').send({ ...validPayload, nonce: 'testnonce' });
    expect(res.status).toBe(409);
  });

  it('should return 400 for unknown model version', async () => {
    const res = await request(app).post('/cca_score/validate').send({ ...validPayload, model_version: 'v99.0' });
    expect(res.status).toBe(400);
    expect(res.body.error).toBe('UNKNOWN_MODEL_VERSION');
  });

  it('should return 400 for clock skew exceeding tolerance', async () => {
    const res = await request(app).post('/cca_score/validate').send({ ...validPayload, client_timestamp: Date.now() - 10 * 60 * 1000 });
    expect(res.status).toBe(400);
    expect(res.body.error).toBe('CLOCK_SKEW');
  });

  it('should return 400 for out-of-bounds score', async () => {
    const res = await request(app).post('/cca_score/validate').send({ ...validPayload, cca_score: 150 });
    expect(res.status).toBe(400);
    expect(res.body.error).toBe('INVALID_SCORE');
  });

  it('should return 409 for score mismatch with cached value', async () => {
    await redis.set('cca_score:user123', 50);
    const res = await request(app).post('/cca_score/validate').send({ ...validPayload, cca_score: 80 });
    expect(res.status).toBe(409);
  });

  it('should return 401 for invalid signature', async () => {
    const res = await request(app).post('/cca_score/validate').send({ ...validPayload, signature: 'invalid' });
    expect(res.status).toBe(401);
  });

  it('should return 200 for valid request', async () => {
    const res = await request(app).post('/cca_score/validate').send(validPayload);
    expect(res.status).toBe(200);
  });
});
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes understanding of secure multi-tenant design, auditable operations, and basic access control in a beginner-friendly setting.

## Key Concepts

- JWT-based auth with tenant_id boundaries
- Row-Level Security or tenant-scoped data stores
- Immutable/append-only audit log with canonical fields
- Model versioning exposure and validation
- End-to-end test strategy for security and data isolation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo middleware to verify JWT and enforce tenant boundary
function authorize(req) {
  const token = req.headers['authorization'];
  const payload = verifyJwt(token);
  if (!payload || payload.tenant_id !== req.params.tenant_id) throw new Error('Unauthorized');
  return payload;
}
```

